## 1. What We Are Building

A **Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)** system that:
1. Ingests every document in the archive
2. Breaks each document into labelled chunks
3. Embeds and indexes all chunks locally (no cloud, no cost, done once)
4. At query time — retrieves the most relevant chunks, feeds them to an LLM
5. The LLM generates a grounded answer with an exact file + section citation

**Evaluation reality:**
- 40% → scores our `predictions.csv` against 32 reference answers (human reviewed)
- 40% → presentation: how well we explain and demonstrate the system
- 20% → NAPE runs our notebook, checks it finishes within 30 minutes without crashing

