## 3. Document Classification Decision Table

This is the most important decision in the pipeline. Every file in the archive falls into one of two content types:

| Content Type | Description | Files |
|---|---|---|
| **Type A — Narrative Text** | English prose sentences. An LLM can read and answer from these. | Well Summary PDFs |
| **Type B — Number Tables** | Header metadata + columns of depth/angle/coordinate numbers. Only the header is useful text. | All Survey Report PDFs, all no-extension raw files (`_ACTUAL`, `_PLAN`, `_PROTOTYPE`), all `.txt` survey files |

### What We Index From Each File Type

| File | Content Type | What to Index | What to Discard |
|---|---|---|---|
| **DDR HTML** (32 files) | Narrative + structured tables | **Everything** — chunked by named section | Nothing |
| **DDR XML** (32 files) | Same as HTML | **Skip entirely** | Everything |
| **DDR PDF** (32 files) | Same as HTML | **Skip entirely** | Everything |
| **Well Summary PDFs** (21 files) | Type A — narrative | **Full content**, chunked by page | Nothing |
| **Standard Survey Report PDFs** | Type B — number tables | **Page 1 header only** (metadata) | Pages 2+ (pure number rows) |
| **Raw text files** `_ACTUAL`, `_PLAN`, `_PROTOTYPE` (109 files) | Type B — number tables | **Header only** (lines 1 → up to `SURVEY LIST` column headers) | Everything below the column headers |
| **`.txt` survey files** (rare) | Type B — number tables | **Header only** (same rule as raw text) | Everything below the column headers |
| **Relief well PDF summaries** (5 files) | Type A — narrative | **Full content**, chunked by page | Nothing |

### Why We Skip DDR XML and DDR PDF

The 32 DDR reports exist in HTML, XML, and PDF — all with identical content. HTML is the cleanest and most structured format (named CSS classes per section). Indexing all three would triple our chunk count with zero benefit. We pick one format and stick with it: **HTML**.

### Why We Only Index the Header of Survey Files

The header of every survey/prototype/plan/actual file contains all the meaningful text:
```
COMPANY: Statoil Norway
WELL NAME: F-12
WELLBORE NAME: F-12
Kick Off Depth: 145.90m
Survey Name: F12 Rev0.11 CC 240707
Survey Date: 05.08.2008
Surface EW: 435050.210m
Surface NS: 6478566.220m
Bottom Hole MD: 3441.29m
Bottom Hole TVD: 3073.84m
Water Depth: 91.00m
```

The 120+ rows below the header are columns of coordinate numbers that an LLM cannot answer questions from. The header alone can answer questions like "what was the bottom hole depth of F-12?" — which is all we ever need.

**Rule:** Index all lines from line 1 up to (but not including) the row that starts with `MD` or `SURVEY LIST` (the column headers line). This is typically lines 1–38.

