## 4. Chunking Strategy (Per Document Type)

### 4a. DDR HTML Files — Chunk By Named Section

The HTML DDRs are structured into clearly named sections using CSS class `TextHeader`. Each section becomes **one chunk**.

Sections in a typical DDR:
1. **Wellbore Info** (the metadata tables — kick-off depth, water depth, hole diameter, etc.)
2. **Summary of Activities (24 Hours)**
3. **Summary of Planned Activities (24 Hours)**
4. **Survey Station** (table of depth/inclination/azimuth readings)
5. **Operations** (time-stamped activity log table)
6. **Drilling Fluid** (fluid properties table)
7. **Pore Pressure** (pore pressure vs depth table)
8. **Log Information** (wireline logging run details)
9. **Gas Reading Information**
10. **Casing Table** (if present)
11. **Cost / Spread Cost** (if present)
12. **Personnel / POB** (if present)

**Each section = 1 chunk.** A DDR with 10 sections produces 10 chunks.

Metadata attached to every DDR chunk:
```python
{
    "file_name":  "15_9_F_11_B_2013_05_29.html",
    "file_path":  "documents/daily_drilling_reports/Daily_Drilling_Report___HTML_Version/15_9_F_11_B_2013_05_29.html",
    "file_type":  "DDR_HTML",
    "well":       "15/9-F-11 B",
    "date":       "2013-05-29",
    "section":    "Operations"
}
```

### 4b. Well Summary PDFs — Chunk By Page

These are 2–3 pages of narrative text. Each page = 1 chunk.

Metadata:
```python
{
    "file_name":  "WellSummary F-1.pdf",
    "file_path":  "documents/wellbore_files/15_9-F-1/WellSummary F-1.pdf",
    "file_type":  "WELL_SUMMARY_PDF",
    "well":       "F-1",
    "page":       2
}
```

### 4c. Survey / Prototype / Plan / Actual Files — Header Only, 1 Chunk Per File

Extract only the header (everything before the survey data table begins). The whole header is one chunk.

Metadata:
```python
{
    "file_name":  "Volve F_F-12_F-12_F12 Rev011 CC 240707_PLAN",
    "file_path":  "documents/wellbore_files/15_9-F-12/15_9-F-12/Volve F_F-12_F-12_F12 Rev011 CC 240707_PLAN",
    "file_type":  "SURVEY_RAW_TEXT",
    "well":       "F-12",
    "status":     "PLAN",
    "section":    "Header"
}
```

