## 6. The Full Pipeline Architecture

```
PHASE 1 — INGESTION (run once, results saved to disk)
                     ↓
         Step 1: Discover all files
         Walk the archive. Classify each file by type.
         (HTML, PDF, raw text, skip)
                     ↓
         Step 2: Extract text from each file
         HTML  → BeautifulSoup, extract by named section
         PDF   → pdfplumber, extract page by page
         Text  → read_text(), take header only (before SURVEY LIST line)
                     ↓
         Step 3: Attach metadata to every chunk
         file_name, file_path, file_type, well, date, section/page
                     ↓
         Step 4: Embed all chunks
         Use Google Gemini embedding API
         (or sentence-transformers locally if API unavailable)
                     ↓
         Step 5: Save index to disk
         FAISS index + metadata list as JSON → saved as files
         (so the notebook doesn't re-embed on every run)

PHASE 2 — QUERY (run once per question at notebook execution time)
                     ↓
         For each of the 32 questions:
                     ↓
         Step 6: Pre-filter by well + date
         Parse the question text. If it mentions a specific well
         (e.g. "15/9-F-11 B") and a specific date ("2013-05-29"),
         filter the chunk list to only those matching chunks FIRST.
         This narrows the search space dramatically.
                     ↓
         Step 7: Semantic search
         Embed the question. Find top 3 most similar chunks
         from the filtered set using FAISS.
                     ↓
         Step 8: Build LLM prompt
         System: "Answer ONLY from the provided document context.
                  If the archive does not support an answer, say so.
                  Always cite the source file and section."
         Context: top 3 retrieved chunks (with their metadata)
         Question: the question text
                     ↓
         Step 9: Call LLM (Gemini API)
         Temperature = 0 (deterministic answers)
                     ↓
         Step 10: Extract answer, evidence, confidence
         Parse LLM response.
         Evidence = file_name + section/page from chunk metadata.
         Confidence = 1.0 if direct match, 0.5 if inferred, blank if abstaining.
                     ↓
         Step 11: Write row to predictions.csv
         question_id, answer, evidence, confidence
```

