## 7. The Retrieval Filter Strategy

This is the key optimization that separates a good system from a great one.

**Most of the 32 questions explicitly name a well and a date.** For example:

> *"On well 15/9-F-11 B, what was the density of the NaCl brine sampled at the flowline at 18:00 on 2013-06-28?"*

We already know:
- Well: `15/9-F-11 B`
- Date: `2013-06-28`
- Section most likely: `Drilling Fluid`

Before doing any embedding-based search, **filter chunks** to only those where:
- `metadata["well"]` matches `15/9-F-11 B`
- `metadata["date"]` matches `2013-06-28`

This reduces the search space from ~491 chunks down to ~10 chunks (just the sections of that one DDR). The semantic search then runs on 10 chunks, not 491. Result: faster, more accurate, no noise.

**For questions without a specific date** (e.g. multi-document or cross-well questions), skip the date filter and filter only by well or just do full-archive search.

