## 8. Handling Special Cases

### T2-027 — The Abstention Question
> *"What did the daily drilling report for well 15/9-F-14 on 2013-06-10 say about operations?"*

There is no DDR for well 15/9-F-14 in the archive. When the pre-filter step finds zero matching chunks for this well + date combination, the system should:
- Return: `answer = "No daily drilling report for well 15/9-F-14 on 2013-06-10 exists in the supplied archive."
- `confidence = 1.0` (a correct abstention earns full marks under the rubric)
- `evidence = "document_manifest.csv — no document found for this well/date"`

### Multi-document Questions (e.g. T2-017, T2-019, T2-022)
Some questions ask you to compare or sequence across multiple wells/dates. For these:
- Run the retrieval separately for each well/date mentioned
- Concatenate the top chunks from each
- Let the LLM synthesise the combined answer

### Questions About Personnel/Cost (e.g. T2-025, T2-026, T2-030)
These fields are present in DDR HTML files in sections like "Cost Summary", "Spread Cost", or "Personnel". The section-based chunking ensures these are captured as their own chunks with clear labels.

