## 9. Tools and Libraries

| Task | Tool | Why |
|---|---|---|
| HTML parsing | `BeautifulSoup4` + `lxml` | Structured extraction by CSS class |
| PDF text extraction | `pdfplumber` | Clean text from digital PDFs (not scanned) |
| Embeddings | `Google Gemini API` (`models/text-embedding-004`) | We have an API key; high quality |
| Vector index | `FAISS` (via `faiss-cpu`) | Local, fast, no server, saves to disk |
| LLM generation | `Google Gemini API` (`gemini-1.5-flash` or `gemini-2.0-flash`) | Temperature=0 for deterministic answers |
| Metadata storage | `JSON` file on disk | Paired with FAISS index |
| Output | `pandas` + `csv` | Write `predictions.csv` |

**Why FAISS over ChromaDB or Pinecone?**  
FAISS is local, requires no server or internet connection during the notebook run, and easily handles 491 chunks in milliseconds. The judges run our notebook offline — FAISS is the safest choice.

